# Normalize line endings in the repository, and keep the VBS assets byte-exact.
#
# Why this matters here: the VBScript assets are staged to disk by the plugin
# with FORCED CRLF because WSH reads .vbs as ANSI and mis-parses bare LF
# sources. The staging step is therefore independent of how the file sits in
# the repository, and tying the assets to LF in the index (not CRLF that a
# Windows checkout would materialize) keeps every clone identical.
#
# `-text` on the .vbs files means "never convert these": whatever bytes are
# committed are the bytes checked out, on any platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.vbs -text

# Binary artifacts, if one is ever added by accident.
*.bmp -text
*.SLDPRT -text
*.SLDASM -text
*.SLDDRW -text
